# TLS mode `internal-ca`: Caddy issues the site certificate from its local CA.
#
# This is the fallback when the organization has no internal CA. It is not a
# temporary self-signed leaf: the local CA is persistent state in the
# `caddy_data` volume, and every client must trust its root certificate before
# the site is usable. The root CA private key never leaves that volume and must
# never be copied into this repository or an image.
#
# Root certificate path inside the container:
#   /data/caddy/pki/authorities/local/root.crt
# Distribution to clients is an IT decision (for example Group Policy). Do not
# enable strict certificate validation in a browser fleet until it is installed.
tls internal
